Within the context of the bag model, we investigate the semileptonic decay processes of singly and doubly charmed heavy spin-1/2 baryons into various light baryons accompanied by a lepton and an anti-neutrino. Our calculations reveal that the decay rates of $\Xi_{cc}^{++}$ into $p l  ar{
u}$ and $\Xi_{cc}^{++}$ into $\Lambda l  ar{
u}$ are significantly high, with the rates of $B(\Xi_{cc}^{++} 	o p l  ar{
u})$ and $B(\Xi_{cc}^+ 	o \Lambda l  ar{
u})$ being approximately $10^{-3}$ and $10^{-3}$, respectively. Furthermore, we have calculated the branching ratios for the decays of $\Xi_{cc}^{++}$ into $p l  ar{
u}$ and $\Xi_{cc}^+ 	o p l  ar{
u}$, which are found to be $B(\Xi_{cc}^{++} 	o p l  ar{
u}) \simeq 0.7$ and $B(\Xi_{cc}^+ 	o p l  ar{
u}) \simeq 0.7$.
